WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.918
- So we wanna put
our guest to work.

00:00:01.918 --> 00:00:05.755
Champ Bailey. Top-three,
top-five corner all time?

00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:08.299
- Damn. I think he's
in the top-five discussion.

00:00:08.299 --> 00:00:10.468
I mean, I'm not just gonna go
out crazy and say top three.

00:00:10.468 --> 00:00:11.803
- Hall of Famer?
- Hall of Famer.

00:00:11.803 --> 00:00:13.346
- Hall of Famer. Get him in, get him in.
- Hands down.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.515
- Come on, guys.
You can exaggerate a little.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.933
- Only DB I ever
practiced against

00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:18.810
that actually scared me
in practice.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.021
- There's a lotta good wide
receivers in the league right now.

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:24.107
I wanna know
how you'd cover them.

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:26.401
First one: Tyreek Hill.

00:00:26.401 --> 00:00:27.986
So, you're Tyreek Hill.
Step to the line.

00:00:27.986 --> 00:00:29.988
- Oh, you know me.
I'm Tyreek Hill, all right.

00:00:29.988 --> 00:00:31.239
- You're Tyreek Hill? OK.

00:00:31.239 --> 00:00:32.741
- Yeah. You still
gonna get up there?

00:00:32.741 --> 00:00:34.367
- Really?
- Absolutely.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.745
I mean, we're both fast.
I mean, we're both fast.

00:00:36.745 --> 00:00:40.040
I won't do this every play,
but I gotta get in your face.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.624
I gotta let you know I'm here.
- Right.

00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:43.752
- I mean, that's my bread
and butter, bump-and-run.

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:45.462
Now, I'm not stupid.
- Right.

00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:47.213
- This boy runs a 4.2,
maybe a 4.1

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:47.797
- This boy runs a 4.2,
maybe a 4.1

00:00:47.797 --> 00:00:50.216
so I'm aware of that
before I play him.

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.677
So my idea of playing him
from the line of scrimmage

00:00:52.677 --> 00:00:54.387
is I gotta stay
in front of him.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.723
You hear this old cliche:
"Get your hands on him."

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:59.350
Man, forget that. It's not about
gettin' your hands on him.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.061
It's about stayin'
in front of him

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.812
makin' it hard
for him to get there.

00:01:02.812 --> 00:01:04.481
That's the easy one.
That's the one they want.

00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:05.190
That's the easy one.
That's the one they want.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.775
- And you're not gonna try
to jam him?

00:01:06.775 --> 00:01:07.984
- Of course I'm gonna try
to jam him.

00:01:07.984 --> 00:01:08.276
- OK, I thought
you weren't sure.

00:01:08.276 --> 00:01:08.943
- OK, I thought
you weren't sure.

00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:11.112
- No, the hands are secondary.
- I think you're crazy, Champ.

00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:13.239
- The hands are secondary.
So I gotta stay on top of him.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.700
If he wants to run
a 15-yard comeback, curl,
you can have that.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.619
I'mma come down.
I'mma pound you all day.

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:18.161
I'mma come down.
I'mma pound you all day.

00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:20.330
- All right. I'm going time out–
- Right.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:23.208
- Because I believe you've seen the film.
- Yeah.

00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:26.127
- I think a lot of corners have thought
that with Tyreek Hill this year.

00:01:26.127 --> 00:01:26.169
- I think a lot of corners have thought
that with Tyreek Hill this year.
- Yeah.
- And that first–

00:01:26.169 --> 00:01:27.170
- Yeah.
- And that first–

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:27.212
- Yeah.
- And that first–
- We're talking about me though, right?

00:01:27.212 --> 00:01:28.463
- We're talking about me though, right?

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:30.715
- I know I'm talking about you.
- Set him straight!

00:01:30.715 --> 00:01:32.217
- I know this–
- Just want to be clear.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:38.431
but if he did open up on you and
it looked even faster than it was on film.

00:01:38.473 --> 00:01:43.019
Are you coming out earlier? I'm just saying,
like, I haven't seen anyone in the NFL–

00:01:43.019 --> 00:01:47.482
So you're saying that if my film study
didn't show the real speed or I didn't feel it

00:01:47.524 --> 00:01:49.776
and now I'm surprised by–
- Yes. And you got out there

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.528
and he was faster than you
thought he was gonna be?

00:01:51.528 --> 00:01:52.570
- And that happened before.

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:53.988
DeSean Jackson. You know, fast–

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.740
One of the fastest guys I've seen.
- Right.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.409
- Probably fastest I've ever covered.
- Right.

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:01.538
- He– he blew past me on the
first play and I'm chasing.

00:02:01.538 --> 00:02:03.957
I'm like, "Oh my god, this guy's faster than I thought."
- Yeah.

00:02:03.998 --> 00:02:06.626
- I played off him a little more than I wanted to but–
- Okay.

00:02:06.668 --> 00:02:10.046
- At the same time, I still got up in
his face when I had the chance.

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:12.465
You know, it's just being aware
of what the situations are.

00:02:12.507 --> 00:02:14.300
There's a lot of layers to it, man.
- Yes.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.677
I could go on and on about–

00:02:15.718 --> 00:02:16.344
- Let's do another one: Antonio Brown.
- OK.

00:02:16.344 --> 00:02:17.720
- Let's do another one: Antonio Brown.
- OK.

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:19.430
- There's part of me
that believes

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.851
that if you saw Antonio Brown,
it's lockup status.

00:02:22.851 --> 00:02:24.060
that if you saw Antonio Brown,
it's lockup status.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.813
It's "I gotta get my hands on him
big-time." Super-physical.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.106
Am I right?
- You're right.

00:02:28.106 --> 00:02:29.774
I'mma tell you
why you're right.

00:02:29.774 --> 00:02:31.359
Because film study tells me—

00:02:31.359 --> 00:02:33.653
this is what I know because
I've played against him

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.613
I've seen him
throughout the years.

00:02:35.613 --> 00:02:37.532
He has a hard time
with big, long corners.

00:02:37.532 --> 00:02:39.367
- Right.
- Richard Sherman gives him hell.

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:40.535
- Hell.
- Hell.

00:02:40.535 --> 00:02:42.203
- So I'm aware of that.

00:02:42.203 --> 00:02:43.705
- And no one factors this into
the best wide receiver—
- Jalen Ramsey is givin' him hell.

00:02:43.705 --> 00:02:45.874
- Give him hell, you know?
It's hard for him.

00:02:45.874 --> 00:02:47.542
And why is it hard for him?

00:02:47.542 --> 00:02:49.210
Because they stay in front
of him, they make it hard.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.461
He can't run around him

00:02:50.461 --> 00:02:52.255
he can't just wiggle
and just go.

00:02:52.255 --> 00:02:54.299
The tape will tell you
everything. Tape doesn't lie.

00:02:54.299 --> 00:02:54.924
- I agree.

00:02:54.924 --> 00:02:58.344
