with a Julio for that long?

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.013
Like, is that
physically demanding?

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:02.348
Like, are you exhausted more
after that game

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.434
than after a game
against Antonio Brown?

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:06.477
- You know, a guy like that,
he's bigger

00:03:06.477 --> 00:03:08.521
so he's not gonna have
the same release

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:11.649
but he's stronger, so your feet
really play a role there

00:03:11.649 --> 00:03:13.359
because if you're just standing
there with your arms out like this—

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.612
- Oh, you're getting tossed.
- He's just, you know, a la Brandon Marshall.

00:03:15.612 --> 00:03:16.654
- Oh, you're getting tossed.
- He's just, you know, a la Brandon Marshall.

00:03:16.654 --> 00:03:18.615
- Or he's gonna give
you the jerk-through.

00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:20.366
- I mean, yeah.
These guys grab you.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.743
They want you to grab 'em.

00:03:21.743 --> 00:03:21.951
They want you to grab 'em.

00:03:21.951 --> 00:03:23.912
But I'll try to get
my hands on 'em

00:03:23.912 --> 00:03:26.122
but it's really more
about my positioning.

00:03:26.122 --> 00:03:28.917
You know, I just wanna make sure
that I have a strong foundation

00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:31.920
because they'll throw you by,
they'll grab your helmet.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.797
I mean, it doesn't matter.
Fitzgerald, he's the king of that.

00:03:34.797 --> 00:03:36.591
He'll grab you, pull you.
- Right.

00:03:36.591 --> 00:03:38.593
- And another thing you have to
worry about is blocking.

00:03:38.593 --> 00:03:40.762
Those dudes block
their asses off.

00:03:40.762 --> 00:03:44.182
- Of all the guys right now,
whether it's Odell, Julio

00:03:44.182 --> 00:03:47.727
Keenan Allen, Antonio Brown,
DeAndre Hopkins, Tyreek Hill

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:51.022
which one are you goin'
"60 minutes—

00:03:51.022 --> 00:03:53.149
I could get anything,
I could get everything

00:03:53.149 --> 00:03:55.860
that's gonna cause me
to earn my paycheck the most?"

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:59.155
- Well, I think, uh, Odell
is probably the scariest

00:03:59.155 --> 00:04:02.200
because his run after the catch
is superb.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.868
I mean, his first step
is superb.

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:03.993
I mean, his first step
is superb.

00:04:03.993 --> 00:04:06.037
There's really not a lot
of weaknesses in his game.

00:04:06.037 --> 00:04:07.247
- Yeah.
- He can catch everything.

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:07.956
- Yeah.
- He can catch everything.

00:04:07.956 --> 00:04:09.624
You know, his route
running is excellent.

00:04:09.624 --> 00:04:11.000
- We've been saying this
for years.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.043
- Oh, yeah?
- But people haven't believed us.

00:04:12.043 --> 00:04:13.294
- Oh, yeah?
- But people haven't believed us.

00:04:13.294 --> 00:04:14.879
- Yeah, well, people
wanna hate on Odell.

00:04:14.879 --> 00:04:17.090
- I get it. I mean,
he's a little flamboyant.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.425
You know, he likes
the limelight, like to dance.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.719
You know, so what?
- But he's still awesome.
- What does he do between the lines?

00:04:21.719 --> 00:04:23.763
- Right, right.
